Groupoids of \uline{Teichmüller}

1) Topological groupoids $\boxed{S\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}}$.
(\uline{special oriented topological Teichmüller groupoid})

Objects: pairs $(X,S)$
\[
\left|\begin{array}{l}
X\ \text{compact \uline{oriented} surface with boundary}\\
S\subset\partial X\quad\text{finite subset of the boundary}
\end{array}\right.
\]
Morphisms $(X,S)\longrightarrow(X',S')$: isotopy classes of isomorphisms

\deleted{\unsure{Variants|Three}} \uline{Variants}

$1^\circ)$ $S=\varnothing$ we write $\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}$ open subgroupoid.
(\uline{\deleted{\unsure{oriented}} oriented topological Teichmüller groupoid})

$\unsure{2^\circ|1^\circ})$ $\boxed{S\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}^\pm}$ same objects, but more arrows:
isotopy classes of homeomorphisms $(X,S)\xrightarrow{\sim}(X',S')$, not necessarily preserving the orientation.

We have
\diagram{\begin{tikzcd}[ampersand replacement=\&,column sep=large]
S\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}^\pm \arrow[r,"\unsure{\chi|\varepsilon}","\text{(signature)}"']
\& \deleted{\unsure{\mathfrak G}}\ \substack{\text{\deleted{one-object} groupoid}\\
\text{defined by the group}\\
\pm1,\ \text{denoted }[\pm1]}
\end{tikzcd}}
the \deleted{kernel} \deleted{is} (the fibre category) is $S\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}$

$2^\circ)$ $(X,\Sigma,S)$, with
\[
\left|\begin{array}{l}
X\ \text{compact with oriented boundary}\\
\Sigma\ \text{\deleted{closed} \inserted{compact} submanifold of dimension $1$}\\
\qquad\text{of }X\setminus\partial X\\
S\subset\Sigma\cup\partial X\quad\text{finite subset}
\end{array}\right.
\]
morphisms: isotopy classes of homeomorphisms preserving the orientation.
Notation $\mathcal T\deleted{\unsure{S}}\inserted{D}_{\mathrm{top}}$
($D$ initial of dévissage \deleted{``\unsure{wild}''}):
``\uline{oriented dévissed topological Teichmüller groupoid}''.

\uline{Note well}
\[
S\mathcal T_{\mathrm{top}}\subset S\mathcal TD_{\mathrm{top}}
\qquad
\substack{\text{open immersion}\\(\deleted{\text{full embedding}})}
\]
\[
\substack{\Vert\\\text{subgroupoid of objects such that }\Sigma=\varnothing}
\]

$3^\circ)$ We define in the $=$ way $\mathcal TS_{\mathrm{top}}^\pm$
(\uline{bioriented dévissed topological Teichmüller groupoid})
